  "notes": "A stingray from above, its axis the V0-V3 diagonal: snout at V0 (three rays meet nose to nose), the whip tail with its spine at V3, the wing tips out on e1 and e4. Mirror-symmetric as the C3 relations allow (e0 straight, e4 = e2 with v negated). e2 runs from the rear rim of the right wing down the tail; turned a third about V2 it is e1, so the dent where the tail leaves the disc is the bulge of the wing's front rim. v1 = (0.5, 0) pulls V3 out for a long tail.",
